<title>BANGLADESH: Chittagong handles 15,659 T of cargo in 24 hours.</title>
<headline>Chittagong handles 15,659 T of cargo in 24 hours.</headline>
<dateline>CHITTAGONG, Bangladesh 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bangladesh's main Chittagong port handled 15,659 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours ending at 1.00 p.m. (0700 GMT) on Monday</p>
<p>compared with 19,756 tonnes in the same period on Sunday, port</p>
<p>officials said.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					Monday		  Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo		   2,702		   3,433</p>
<p>    Import cargo		  12,957		  16,323</p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Chittagong port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	   Tonnes     Ship</p>
<p>Berthing</p>
<p>Cement 8,707 Zang San 22/10</p>
<p>High Speed Diesel     20,378     Primar	     23/10</p>
<p>Fertiliser		11,000     Hyok STN	   25/10</p>
<p>Wheat		     25,000     Prospathia	 7/11</p>
<p>-- Dhaka Newsroom 880-2-506363</p>
</text>
